<title>UK: Commercial Union up, vague bid hopes linger.</title>
<headline>Commercial Union up, vague bid hopes linger.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-08-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in insurer Commercial Union bucked a market downtrend, rising amid lingering bid hopes although these were dismissed by market makers as increasingly vague.</p>
<p>Commercial Union was up 12-1/2 pence at 749-1/2 but turnover was light at just over 258,000 shares and dealers paid little attention to the merger hopes.</p>
<p>Earlier this month, Commercial Union ruled out any merger when the composite insurer reported its first-half results.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
